          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Solve the following for ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "0^{\\circ}\\leq\\theta\\leq360^{\\circ}",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ".",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p29-q5",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\theta=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=0^{\\circ},180^{\\circ},360^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "On the unit circle, $\\sin\\theta$ is the $y$-coordinate. It is zero on the $x$-axis. Both endpoints are included.\n\n$$\\theta=0^{\\circ},180^{\\circ},360^{\\circ}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q6",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\cos\\theta=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=90^{\\circ},270^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "On the unit circle, $\\cos\\theta$ is the $x$-coordinate. It is zero on the $y$-axis.\n\n$$\\theta=90^{\\circ},270^{\\circ}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q7",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\tan\\theta=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=0^{\\circ},180^{\\circ},360^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}&=0\\\\\\sin\\theta&=0\\\\\\theta&=0^{\\circ},180^{\\circ},360^{\\circ}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nAt each solution, $\\cos\\theta\\neq0$, so tangent is defined.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q8",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\theta=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=90^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "The unit-circle $y$-coordinate is $1$ only at the top of the circle.\n\n$$\\theta=90^{\\circ}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q9",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\cos\\theta=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=0^{\\circ},360^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "The unit-circle $x$-coordinate is $1$ on the positive $x$-axis. Both endpoints are included.\n\n$$\\theta=0^{\\circ},360^{\\circ}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q10",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\theta=-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=270^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "The unit-circle $y$-coordinate is $-1$ only at the bottom of the circle.\n\n$$\\theta=270^{\\circ}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q11",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$\\cos\\theta=-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=180^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "The unit-circle $x$-coordinate is $-1$ on the negative $x$-axis.\n\n$$\\theta=180^{\\circ}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q12",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$\\sec\\theta=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "No solution.",
          "worked": "$$\\sec\\theta=\\frac{1}{\\cos\\theta},\\qquad\\cos\\theta\\neq0.$$\n\nThe numerator is $1$, so this fraction cannot equal zero. There is no solution.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q13",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "No solution.",
          "worked": "$$\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta=\\frac{1}{\\sin\\theta},\\qquad\\sin\\theta\\neq0.$$\n\nThe numerator is $1$, so this fraction cannot equal zero. There is no solution.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q14",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "j",
        "prompt": "$\\cot\\theta=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p29-q14-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\theta=90^{\\circ},270^{\\circ}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p29-q14-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\cot\\theta=\\frac{\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}&=0\\\\\\cos\\theta&=0\\\\\\theta&=90^{\\circ},270^{\\circ}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nAt both solutions, $\\sin\\theta\\neq0$, so cotangent is defined. Tangent is undefined there.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q15",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "k",
        "prompt": "$\\sec\\theta=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=0^{\\circ},360^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{\\cos\\theta}&=1\\\\\\cos\\theta&=1\\\\\\theta&=0^{\\circ},360^{\\circ}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nBoth endpoints are included, and cosine is nonzero at each.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q16",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "l",
        "prompt": "$\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=90^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{\\sin\\theta}&=1\\\\\\sin\\theta&=1\\\\\\theta&=90^{\\circ}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nHere $\\sin\\theta=1\\neq0$, so cosecant is defined.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q17",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "m",
        "prompt": "$\\sec\\theta=-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=180^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{\\cos\\theta}&=-1\\\\\\cos\\theta&=-1\\\\\\theta&=180^{\\circ}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nHere $\\cos\\theta=-1\\neq0$, so secant is defined.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q18",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "n",
        "prompt": "$\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta=-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=270^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{\\sin\\theta}&=-1\\\\\\sin\\theta&=-1\\\\\\theta&=270^{\\circ}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nHere $\\sin\\theta=-1\\neq0$, so cosecant is defined.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      }
    ]
  },
